  "body": "## Finding description and impact\n\nUnable to send the StakingManager contract the native token HYPE without triggering the stake() function. This makes it impossible `confirmWithdrawals` since the contract will automatically stake funds when they are withdrawn from the validator.\n\n```solidity\n   receive() external payable {\n        // Simply call the stake function\n        stake();\n    }\n```\n\nSIDE NOTE: This was undetected in the tests because the Foundry cheat code `deal` was used to transfer HYPE which did not trigger the `receive` function of the contract.\n\n## Recommended mitigation steps\n\nAn easy fix is to add a payable function like `depositWithdrawalFunds` that will accept funds withdrawn from a validator. No other logic changes need to be made.\n```solidity\n  function depositWithdrawalFunds() public payable {\n        //do nothing, just accept the funds\n    } \n```",
  "proof_of_concept": "Place the following PoC inside the existing test file `StakingManager.t.sol` \n\nThis test will demonstrate that when the user tries to `confirmWithdrawal` it will revert with `Insufficient contract balance` even after sending the contract the withdraw amount.\n\n```solidity\n     function test_unable_to_receive_withdrawal_funds() public {\n        // Setup initial stake and withdrawal\n        uint256 stakeAmount = 1 ether;\n        vm.startPrank(manager);\n        validatorManager.activateValidator(validator);\n        validatorManager.setDelegation(address(stakingManager), validator);\n        vm.stopPrank();\n\n        vm.deal(user, stakeAmount);\n        vm.prank(user);\n        stakingManager.stake{value: stakeAmount}();\n\n        // Approve and queue withdrawal\n        vm.startPrank(user);\n        kHYPE.approve(address(stakingManager), stakeAmount);\n        // Store the withdrawalId (should be 0 for first withdrawal)\n        uint256 withdrawalId = 0;\n        stakingManager.queueWithdrawal(stakeAmount);\n        vm.stopPrank();\n\n        // below is the originally test method for sending the contract eth.\n        // This is not realistic, since it doesn't trigger the receive function\n        //vm.deal(address(stakingManager), stakeAmount);\n\n        // Set withdrawal delay to 0 to allow immediate confirmation\n        vm.prank(manager);\n        stakingManager.setWithdrawalDelay(0);\n\n        StakingManager.WithdrawalRequest memory request = stakingManager.withdrawalRequests(user, withdrawalId);\n        uint256 hypeAmount = request.hypeAmount;\n\n        //ensure the contract should have enough funds to process the withdrawal\n        //@audit this will trigger the receive function and be routed to stake the msg.value\n        //simulate sending the ETH to the contract after it is withdrawn from a validator\n        address withdrawFunder = makeAddr(\"withdrawFunder\");\n        vm.deal(withdrawFunder, hypeAmount);\n        vm.prank(withdrawFunder);\n        address(stakingManager).call{value: hypeAmount}(\"\");\n\n        // Attempt to confirm the withdrawal\n        vm.prank(user);\n        // This will revert since the transferred funds were automatically staked.\n        // The contract will  not have enough funds to process the withdrawal\n        vm.expectRevert(\"Insufficient contract balance\");\n        stakingManager.confirmWithdrawal(withdrawalId);\n    }\n\n```",
